- op: discuss  # 34eb
  at: '2026-08-01T01:29:18Z'  # 34eb
  by: agent  # 34eb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 34eb
  clock: 8  # 34eb
  nonce: 34eb  # 34eb
  message: "PYTHON PILOT LANDED (PR #137). The blocking fact now exists; the item is\nunparked and re-scoped to the producer sweep.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `Symbol.meta[\"constructed_from\"]` records the callee a variable\nis bound to, qualification intact:\n\n    app = FastAPI()                        -> constructed_from = \"FastAPI\"\n    app = fastapi.FastAPI()                -> constructed_from = \"fastapi.FastAPI\"\n    Base = declarative_base()              -> constructed_from = \"declarative_base\"\n    TIMEOUT = 30                           -> (no key)\n    app = factories['web']()               -> (no key)\n\nRegistered on the `symbol_meta` axis; `docs/schema.json` regenerated.\n\nTHE DECISIVE PROPERTY, ASSERTED RATHER THAN INFERRED: the matcher needed NO\nchange. `Pattern.meta_match` already takes a {key: regex} map over\n`Symbol.meta`, so a framework YAML can key on this today. Pinned by\n`test_meta_match_selects_a_constructed_object` in hypergumbo-core.\n\nWHY NOT THE OTHER TWO HOMES. Both cost an ADR ruling this one does not:\n  * a result-position `UsageContext` widens `symbol_ref` from \"the symbol\n    being used\" to \"the symbol produced by this call\" and adds a fifth\n    pattern category to ADR-3ccc, whose status is already Implemented;\n  * a new/widened edge is ADR-0023's territory.\n`Symbol.meta` mirrors `meta.base_classes` — both record what type a symbol\nrelates to, as metadata a linker can later promote to edges if a consumer\never needs to traverse it. Nobody has asked to traverse it yet, which is why\npromoting now would be speculative.\n\nTHREE DELIBERATE NARROWINGS, each guarded by a test:\n  1. Only a call result is stamped. Stamping every variable would make the\n     key useless as a filter.\n  2. Factory and constructor calls are treated identically. Static analysis\n     cannot distinguish them, and asserting \"this is a class\" would be a\n     guess dressed as data.\n  3. A computed callee records NOTHING. `factories[key]()` has no dotted\n     name; emitting a partial one would let a YAML match on a fiction, and\n     the miss would be silent. Absence is the honest signal.\n\nFOUND WHILE TESTING, and worth knowing before writing any YAML against this:\n`meta_match` applies `regex.match`, not `regex.search`. The natural-looking\n`(^|\\.)FastAPI$` SILENTLY FAILS on `fastapi.FastAPI` — `^` matches empty at\nposition 0 and the rest cannot then consume the prefix. `(.*\\.)?FastAPI$` is\nthe form that works. Pinned with a tripwire assertion that fires if the\nmatcher ever switches to `search`.\n\nWHAT REMAINS ON THIS ITEM — the producer sweep, unblocked but not started:\n  * Eight more analyzers emit UsageContext (clojure, elixir, go, js_ts, php,\n    ruby, rust, swift) and none stamps `constructed_from`. Each has its own\n    hardcoded call-name allowlist, so this is an N-producer problem that\n    wants a chokepoint, not eight edits.\n  * A parity column over `constructed_from` per language would make the\n    gaps visible the way the interface-dispatch column did — recommended\n    before the sweep, on the evidence of that column finding five causes\n    nobody was looking for.\n  * NO framework YAML keys on this yet. The capability exists and is\n    untested against a real integration; writing one (FastAPI or SQLAlchemy\n    declarative_base) is the cheapest proof that the whole chain works\n    end to end, and should come before the sweep rather than after.\n\nTITLE STILL WRONG. \"Framework matcher lacks call/instantiates/\nconstructor_call entry families\" describes a defect that does not exist —\nthe matcher's call surface predates the filing by four months. Suggested:\n\"constructor/factory bindings are unrecorded, so construction-keyed YAML\npatterns can never match\". Left unchanged pending a decision on whether to\nre-title or close-and-refile."  # 34eb
